claude-agents-indicator (0.3.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * New claude-agents-tray package: the session list as a tray app for KDE,
    GNOME, XFCE, Cinnamon and other desktops with a system tray.
  * The tray app selects the session's tab in tmux, kitty, WezTerm, Ghostty
    and Konsole, and raises its window on Sway, Hyprland, niri, KDE and X11.
  * Show what a waiting session asks for, such as a permission prompt.
  * Read usage limits from a copy of the status line input, without cctop.
  * The tray shows the waiting count as its label and title.
  * New claude-agents-status command for waybar, polybar, i3blocks and tmux,
    once or with --follow.
  * claude-agents-tray --jump goes to the session that needs you, for a
    keyboard shortcut.
  * On KDE, a session with no window opens the agent view.

 -- rezk2ll <6764881+rezk2ll@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0100

